recast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Delaware enters the 2028 presidential race as a modest Democratic-leaning state, carrying an eight-point partisan edge toward Democrats. With the incumbent president term-limited, both parties face open contests, and no candidate has an incumbency advantage. No public polls of the state, expert ratings, or market pricing exist yet, so the forecast rests on the state's underlying partisan lean.\n\nNational headlines remain focused on the unsettled Democratic primary field and early speculation about Republican match-ups, with no Delaware-specific developments. Until polling arrives, the state's fundamentals point to a Democratic advantage that is meaningful but not yet in safe territory, and the wide uncertainty band reflects how much could change once actual campaigns and surveys take shape.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8204, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7838, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7798, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7761, "margin": 8.0}]}